{
  "id": "finite-state-grammar",
  "term": "finite-state grammar",
  "definition": "A finite-state grammar is a rule system used in artificial grammar learning to generate example sequences that people can study and later judge as grammatical or not. In this context, such grammars can differ in complexity, with simpler ones generally being learned more easily than more complex ones.",
